  "title": "Coast Guard Medevacs Heart-Attack Patient From Cruise Ship off N.C.",
  "description": "The Coast Guard medevaced an 81-year-old man Saturday, Nov. 16, 2013, from the Norwegian Breakaway, a 1,063-foot cruise ship, approximately 55 miles southwest of Cape Hatteras, N.C. The Jayhawk helicopter crew arrived on scene, hoisted the man into the helicopter and took him to Sentara Norfolk General Hospital in Norfolk, where he was determined to be in stable condition. U.S. Coast Guard video by Coast Guard Air Station Elizabeth City",
